.TH IDLESCREEN 1 "October 2026" "idlescreen 4.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
idlescreen \- IdleScreen standalone screensaver and idle management suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B idlescreen
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B idlescreen-daemon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBidlescreen\fR is a unified idle management and screensaver suite for Linux Wayland sessions.
It features a zero-CPU event-driven daemon, built-in dynamic ASCII screensaver (37 effects),
and an optional library of 11 mathematical screensavers via \fBidlescreen-extras\fR.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Start the IdleScreen background daemon.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Query daemon state, active inhibitors, and current display status.
.TP
.B preview [\fISAVER\fR]
Preview a screensaver effect immediately in fullscreen or terminal TUI.
.TP
.B list [\-\-json]
List all available screensavers (built-in and installed extras).
.TP
.B set \fISAVER\fR
Set the default screensaver in configuration.
.TP
.B text [\fITEXT\fR | \-\-clear]
Set or clear custom banner text for the ASCII screensaver.
.TP
.B start
Activate the configured screensaver immediately.
.TP
.B stop
Deactivate the currently running screensaver.
.TP
.B inhibit [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\-\- \fICOMMAND\fR...]
Inhibit screensaver activation while a task executes.
.TP
.B inhibitors [\-\-json]
Inspect active idle inhibitors holding back screensaver activation.
.TP
.B service install [\-\-init \fISYSTEM\fR]
Generate and install a user-level service definition for systemd, OpenRC, runit, s6, dinit, or XDG autostart.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-verbose] [\-\-json] [\-\-fix]
Perform system diagnostics, Wayland checks, and optional auto-remediation (\fB\-\-fix\fR).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in \fB~/.config/idlescreen/config.toml\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd (1)
